{"id":"315a8ca2-ab63-436a-9c76-10541e87c870","object":"chat.completion","created":1788900730,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Record-form `parallel` type-checks, but the checker taints the secret at the flow level. I need to learn exactly which construction keeps `appName` out of the tainted channel before spending more proposal attempts — simulating candidate shapes in memory.","reasoning_content":"Interesting: the record form type-checked (no unknown member diagnostics, no "declaration destructuring" issue), so `parallel({ appName: ..., apiSecret: ... })` with `values.apiSecret` member access is valid. But now ZTS400: secret data flows into response body.

