What if we do the parallel in the branch: first read both concurrently... hmm, must still return 503 when API_SECRET unset and otherwise return app name from the SAME parallel call result — the appName lives on the tainted object.

Unless... the taint isn't object-level but the checker flagged something else: maybe `apiSecret` narrowing `!== undefined` then... we don't use it. What about `name = values.appName ?? ""` — is appName undefined handling OK.

Alternatively maybe the issue is that env("API_SECRET") reads by ITSELF inside parallel object literal: parallel may evaluate each thunk as concurrent "job" whose return taints... hmm.

